            <ArticleTitle>Mitochondrial metabolism in infarcting myocardium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>257-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The isolation medium plays an important part in the assessment of mitochondrial damage following coronary artery ligation. Albumin added to either isolation or incubation medium can protect. A depression of oxygen uptake is found only after prolonged ischemia or in a simple incubation medium. Hence mitochondrial oxygen wastage probably occurs in the infarction process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
